From ebd9d3dbe5fd1a8ee211282971493fd65f506a97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kiran Konathala <kiran@example.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:01:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fabric: add Linux ConnectX-7 dual-rail RoCE TP=2 driver and
 GB10 CUDA kernel

- Add zig/src/fabric/roce_linux.zig implementing ConnectX-7 dual-rail RoCE TP=2 driver via libibverbs.
- Add zig/src/native/cuda_roce.cu GB10 (sm_121) PTX all-gather kernel with non-blocking doorbells.
- Add docs/receipts/roce-linux-tp2.md with hardware benchmark receipts on 2x GB10 (14.87 us latency, 15.24 GB/s saturation, 100% byte exactness).
- Verify zero lean_check.py problems added over baseline.
- Tracks native GLM CUDA multi-node support for #593.
